# A lambda bound to a name gives its parameter no type, nothing is annotated, and the binding
# supplies no expected type — `len(s)` accepts every sized type, so `s` is genuinely unknown.
# This used to emit `var g = s => ...`, which C# rejects with CS8917 behind SPY0908 (#1212).
def main():
    g = lambda s: len(s) + 100
    print(g("abcd"))
